    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Traffic:** submit a single news item or a CSV batch in the app, then wait 15\u201330 seconds. Ten batch rows add one request and ten predictions.\n\n**Counters** reset when the app restarts. Rate panels use a five-minute window and need multiple scrapes. Idle latency/error percentages can be blank. Counts do not measure model accuracy.\n\n**Model evaluation and data drift** remain in the News Signal application. They are not exported as Prometheus metrics in this version. Mean latency is not p95/p99. The existing Prometheus storage controls history retention; Grafana stores dashboards and settings only."
      }
    }
